# Developer Assistance Console (ENT-7)

ENT-7 is locked as completed foundation governance.

1. The console (`GET /dev-console`, route `developer-console.index`) is strictly read-only — never add a non-GET console route.
2. Access is gated by the `view_developer_console` permission; only Super Admin holds it by default.
3. Every console page view must stay audited via `sys_audit_logs` (`DeveloperConsoleService::recordAccess`).
4. All free-text excerpts must pass `SensitiveValueMasker` — never render full KTP/NIK digit runs, credentials, tokens, or environment file contents.
5. Audit payload columns (old/new values) are never rendered in the console.
6. New console panels/exports require masking coverage, permission/audit tests, and a passing `foundation:developer-console-check` first.
7. ENT-5 and ENT-6 stay mandatory: run `php artisan foundation:queue-retry-failed-job-check --strict` and `php artisan foundation:idempotency-outbox-check --strict`.
8. Before later ENT work, run `php artisan foundation:developer-console-check --strict`.
9. Preserve the `queue_retry_governance`, `idempotency_outbox_governance`, and `developer_console_governance` summary sections.
